ps5-iw620-kernel73-compat.patch: build the NXP IW620 Wi-Fi driver on Linux 7.3

Applies to nxp-imx/mwifiex a5fe4e1 (lf-6.18.2_1.0.0) after the four patches
from ps5-linux/ps5-linux-mwifiex 4aff908 that the 7.1.7 Ubuntu Wi-Fi build
also used, in this order: ps5-iw620.patch,
ps5-iw620-cmd-timeout-recover.patch, ps5-iw620-kernel71-compat.patch,
ps5-iw620-rtnl-bounded-wait.patch.
Do not combine it with ps5-iw620-kernel72-compat.patch.

Linux 7.3 changed three things the driver uses. Every change below sits
behind a 7.3.0 version check, so older kernels build exactly as before.

- cfg80211 now chooses the cookie for remain_on_channel and mgmt_tx and
  passes it by value, and remain_on_channel gains an rx_addr argument. The
  driver copies the value into a local variable and no longer makes up its
  own random cookie, so the cookie it reports back is the one cfg80211
  handed out.
- struct cfg80211_ops no longer has probe_client, so
  woal_cfg80211_probe_client and its assignment are compiled out.
- strncpy() is gone from the kernel. moal_main.h maps strncpy to
  woal_strncpy, which keeps strncpy's behaviour: copy at most count bytes,
  stop at the first NUL and zero-fill the rest of the buffer.

With this patch the driver builds against 7.3.0 with objtool on and no
compiler, objtool or modpost warnings. It has not run on hardware yet.
WPA3-SAE association sends its frames through mgmt_tx, so a WPA3 join is the
first thing to check.

